1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,750
Sari runs Arif's method on her own portfolio.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:07,390
Her positions are sealed on her device and only opened inside a secure enclave.

3
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,770
The answer comes back sealed to her alone.

4
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:13,140
Arif never sees her numbers, and she never sees his rules.

5
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:16,120
Next time, she doesn't want to type her positions by hand.

6
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:23,300
So she connects the apps her methods need, from exchanges and wallets to Google Sheets and Docs, with read-only access she can revoke anytime.

7
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:25,560
Her methods also need to remember her rules.

8
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,530
She saves her risk limit as a note.

9
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:32,450
Notes and documents are encrypted on her own device, so our server only ever holds ciphertext.

10
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:38,070
Now Sari wants her AI agent to act on the plan and pay for things, without giving it the keys to everything.

11
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:41,800
She gives the agent a sandbox wallet holding only the limit she chose.

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,520
Every payment it proposes goes to a guard method running inside a NEAR OutLayer enclave on Intel TDX hardware.

13
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:53,030
A private model on NEAR AI Cloud checks the request, and an attestation proves exactly which code ran.

14
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:55,370
A hidden instruction tries to drain the wallet.

15
00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:56,090
Blocked.

16
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:58,400
The safe payment goes through after she approves it.

17
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,220
And if everything else failed, the network itself refuses to spend more than the sandbox holds.

